{"title":"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a991878e9000186fa654fbc0b1b75c902420bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\log_2(\\log_2(x)))=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" />, then how many digits are in the base-ten representation for x?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f49f3d0a95b9980c85f54fc3f28c46556f7bb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 5\\quad \\text{(B) } 7\\quad \\text{(C) } 9\\quad \\text{(D) } 11\\quad \\text{(E) } 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking successive exponentials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39d0fa7e32013bafaf3dbde915bbfe76dc56dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\log_2(x)) = 2^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1da93bec9ba341d8f9045c4526be5c933da40f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(x) = 2^4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55be3cfd5cd97f15a34e61acf561fb842f9d402d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2^{16}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.  Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fce815fabfec5e9b63ac4535065714d3eff58c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10} = 1024 \\approx 10^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a901d5103f4658787ce321610aa348a76ea79fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> so we can approximate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7773d5a51ddd4a4a1e39745637c975318cad914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{16} \\approx 64000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> which has 5 digits.  In general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> has approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf0d3a91d97b319760cdc7ce694b0c7e8d52744b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> digits.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME\" title=\"1993 AHSME\">1993 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti